  ],
  "aliases": [
    "acorn amigurumi",
    "crochet acorn",
    "woodland ornament crochet"
  ],
  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "magic-ring",
      "definition": "An adjustable start loop that closes to leave no hole at the centre of a piece."
    },
    {
      "slug": "amigurumi-decrease",
      "definition": "An invisible decrease worked through the front loops only to reduce stitch count without a visible gap."
    },
    {
      "slug": "back-loop-only",
      "definition": "Working through the back loop of each stitch only, leaving the front loop free and creating a visible ridge on the right side."
    },
    {
      "slug": "slip-stitch-join",
      "definition": "A slip stitch used to close a round invisibly."
    }
  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This tiny acorn is one of the simplest amigurumi in the woodland collection. An oval body forms the nut and a textured cylinder cap sits on top, joined with a chain stitch stalk. Both pieces start with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The finished acorn measures about 7 cm tall including the stalk."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK yarn: 15 g chestnut, 10 g dark brown, 1 g green (for stalk). 3.5 mm crochet hook. Polyester stuffing. Tapestry needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "24 sts × 28 rows = 10 × 10 cm in dc on a 3.5 mm hook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Acorn Body (chestnut)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1: Chain 4. Working along chain: 2 sc in 2nd ch from hook, sc in next 1 ch, 3 sc in last ch, rotate. Along opposite side: sc in next 1 ch, 2 sc in last ch (10 st) (10 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2: Increase 6 stitches evenly around (16 st) (16 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3: Increase 6 stitches evenly around (22 st) (22 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4: Increase 6 stitches evenly around (28 st) (28 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 5: Increase 6 stitches evenly around (34 st) (34 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 6: sc in each st (34 st) (34 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 7: sc in each st (34 st) (34 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 8: sc in each st (34 st) (34 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 9: Decrease 6 stitches evenly around (28 st) (28 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 10: Decrease 6 stitches evenly around (22 st) (22 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 11: Decrease 6 stitches evenly around (16 st) (16 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 12: Decrease 6 stitches evenly around (10 st). FO leaving 15 cm tail for closure. (10 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Acorn Cap (dark brown)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the cap in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "back-loop-only"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "back loops only"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throughout to create the bumpy texture of a real acorn cap. The raised front loops will show on the right side."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1: 6 sc in magic ring (6 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2: [inc] × 6 (12 st) (12 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3: [2 sc, inc] × 6 (18 st) (18 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4: [3 sc, inc] × 6 (24 st) (24 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 5: [4 sc, inc] × 6 (30 st) (30 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 6: [5 sc, inc] × 6 (36 st) (36 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 7: sc in each st (36 st) (36 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 8: sc in each st (36 st). FO leaving 30 cm tail for joining to body. (36 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stalk"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 5 in green. Work 1 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch-join"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "slip stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in each chain. Fasten off, leaving a 10 cm tail for sewing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stuff the body lightly to hold its oval shape. Leave the cap unstuffed. Set the cap base over the top third of the body and sew it down with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "amigurumi-decrease"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "whip stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " all round. Thread the stalk through the cap top and knot it on the inside with a few back stitches."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. The acorn can be made in multiples as props for the squirrel or as Christmas tree decorations by adding a loop of thread at the stalk end."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to make next: the amigurumi-mushroom is another quick woodland accent, or try the amigurumi-squirrel for a creature to pair with your acorn."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}